From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:30:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sep: let an open wait for the
 activation's own open

/dev/sep-bio takes one opener at a time, and the first open of a boot
activates Touch ID inside the open itself: the enclave restore and the
unlock preflight, most of a second. Its opener, omarchy-mac's activation
unit, closes at once afterwards. An open that arrived in that window was
refused with EBUSY, and libfprint takes EBUSY as a reader it cannot use
for the daemon's whole life, so a J604 boot was left without Touch ID
until fprintd exited.

Keep what the holder of the node is doing in a small module the host
tests can build: whether its open is still preparing the node, and
whether that open ran this boot's activation. An open now waits, for at
most 5 s, while the holder is the activation's own open, the same way it
already waits for an outgoing enrol or verify worker. A node still held
after that, or held by anyone else, is refused as before.

This is the kernel half of a race whose user-space half omarchy-mac
0.2.3-2.17 closes by ordering fprintd after the activation.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
